#
# Counter-example for lang:FlagshipScenarioShape: a lang:FlagshipScenario that binds ALL
# links — lang:demonstratedByExample, lang:demonstratedByCompetency,
# lang:guardedByCounterExample, AND lang:enforcesFailureClass — so every sh:minCount
# branch is satisfied, but lang:enforcesFailureClass names lang:Grammar, a real class that
# is NOT a lang:LangConformanceFailure subclass. Only the sh:sparql subclass check fires,
# so validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (and no other finding,
# lang:UnwiredFlagshipScenario): an acceptance scenario whose enforcing failure class is
# not a typed conformance failure is unwired by value, not by cardinality.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecFlagshipNonFailureClass).
@prefix lang: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/lang/> .

ex:nonFailureClassScenario a lang:FlagshipScenario ;
    lang:demonstratedByExample "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-cats-chase-mice.ttl" ;
    lang:demonstratedByCompetency <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/lang/tests/cqDenotationsToFormula> ;
    lang:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/meaning-underspecified-denotation.ttl" ;
    lang:enforcesFailureClass lang:Grammar .
